Survey row 8b (KIT-MACOS-ARM64 section 6): lifts the host refusal "A subdivision surface cannot be baked"
(native/host/host_bake.inc, bake_request) so that the next behaviour of a subdivision-surface bake can be recorded.

SURVEY BUILD ONLY, NEVER PRODUCT CODE. Scratch change for the Apple Silicon feature survey; applied with
`patch -p1 -d <survey copy>` to a git-archive copy of the base tree under native/work/, never to the repository.
Base: branch cycles-with-metal-v5.3.0, commit 0b19d87507ac24f1e55ba6a50d1ac6b05c8d417c (host sources identical to 828f6c2f9).

--- a/native/host/host_bake.inc
+++ b/native/host/host_bake.inc
@@ -57,7 +57,6 @@
   require(request.object, "Bake object handle is not an object");
   request.mesh = dynamic_cast<Mesh *>(request.object->get_geometry());
   require(request.mesh, "Only an object whose geometry is a triangle mesh can be baked");
-  require(request.mesh->get_subdivision_type() == Mesh::SUBDIVISION_NONE, "A subdivision surface cannot be baked", CBC_UNSUPPORTED);
   require(request.mesh->num_triangles() > 0, "The bake mesh has no triangles");
   const char *name = config->uv_attribute;
   request.uv = name && *name ? request.mesh->attributes.find(ustring(name)) : request.mesh->attributes.find(ATTR_STD_UV);
